Check contact readiness without a settling sleep. Check the ended-call
status, history, direction and duration against measured elapsed time,
instead of assuming that the complete call always takes zero seconds.

Exercise cancellation through ordinary, priority and batched store calls.

Make the per-user chat-item TTL examples deterministic: use a large ttl while
setting up and asserting, then drop it to 1 so the items expire synchronously
instead of relying on the periodic cleanup and on how long the (loaded)
builder takes.  The timed-message example uses a ttl comfortably larger than
the assertions.  Give the aborted connection-switch examples a larger settle
delay before reading the persisted chat items.

